# Markdown is NOT formatted by prettier here, and this file is what makes that a decision rather
# than an accident of the lint-staged globs in package.json (which only match js/jsx/ts/tsx/json).
#
# Why: prettier re-aligns every column of a markdown table it touches, so adding two rows to the
# signal table in docs/operations.md rewrites the whole table and buries the change in 36 lines of
# whitespace. The docs here carry the *why* — they are meant to be read in diffs.
*.md

# GENERATED — owned byte-for-byte by scripts/ops/cli-reference.ts, which compares the file on disk
# against what it would emit. Letting prettier reformat it makes the generator and the committed
# file disagree permanently: `cli-reference --check` fails immediately after every commit, because
# lint-staged rewrites the file the generator just wrote. (Measured, not theoretical — this
# happened on the commit that introduced the catalogue.) Regenerate with
# `npm run cli:reference -- --apply` instead.
docs/cli-tools.json
